  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nBooks\nGifts\nThe Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry Chronicle 1954\n£10.00\n\nLow stock, 4 remaining\nThe Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry Chronicle 1954 quantity\nAdd to Cart\n\nCompiled and Edited by Brigadier-General C. G. Higgins, C.M.G., D.S.O., D.L. Volume LVI January to December 1954.\n\nPublished 1955 - Slatter & Rose Oxford. Hardcover.\n\n \n\nContents:\n\nThe Army List -p.1\n\nExtracts from the 'London Gazette' 1954 -p.3\n\nRegular Officers of the Regiment Extra-Regimentally Employed on December 31st, 1954 -p.9\n\nFormer Officers of the Regiment on the Active List December 31st, 1954 -p.11\n\nRecords of the First Battallion -p. 12\n\nSummary of the First Battalion Diary 1954 -p.15\n\nFirst Battalion Letter -p.26\n\nFirst Battalion Records of Sport and Training -p.36\n\nHorses at Osnabruck -p.63\n\nHorse Shows and Hunter Trials 1954 -p.65\n\nRecords of Regimental Headquarters -p.68\n\nRegimental Headquarters Letter -p.69\n\nRecords of the Fourth Battalion -p.74\n\nFourth Battalion Letter -p.78\n\nRegimental Dinner 1954 -p.84\n\n52nd Light Infantry Dinner 1954 -p.85\n\n52nd Light Infantry Luncheon 1954 -p.86\n\n2nd Buckinghamshire Battalion Officers' Dinner  Club -p. 88\n\nPresentation of New Colours to the First Battalion (43rd & 52nd) -p.89\n\nFour Days in Osnabruck, May 1954 -p.99\n\nBritish Social Life in Germany 1954 -p.107\n\nAmerican Citation For Major-General West -p.115\n\nThe Royal Hospital, Chelsea -p.117\n\nPresentation of New Colours to the Fourth Battalion -p.127\n\n'All Right on the Day' -p.136\n\nAdministrative Days -p.140\n\nAn Excercise in the Sub-Arctic -p.149\n\nS. V. I -p.160\n\nGame Shooting in Germany 1954 -p.170\n\nAttachment to the Swiss Army -p.176\n\n Somaliland -p.185\n\nThe Regimental Band -p.191\n\nSerjeants' Mess - First Battalion Plate and Pictures -p.195\n\nLight Infantry Brigade-p.202\n\nHistorical Note on the Use of Colours -p.207\n\nRegimental Cricket Week 1954 -p.212\n\nOld Comrades' Association -p.216\n\n1914 Star Roll -p.218\n\nMarriage -p. 255\n\nObituary -p.256\n\nIndex -p.259\n\nPlease Note: Original copies supplied, all in used but reasonable condition. Copy supplied may vary slightly from the one pictured in terms of wear and aging.\n\n \n\nRelated products\nThe Story of the Oxfordshire Yeomanry – Queen’s Own Oxfordshire Hussars 1798-1998\n£7.95 Read more\nMESOPOTAMIA 1914-15: EXTRACTS FROM A REGIMENTAL OFFICER’S DIARY\n£11.99 Add to cart\nConflict & County\n£5.95 Add to cart\nBugle & Sabre VIII\n£5.00 Add to cart\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
